The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (is_shadow_present_pte(*spte) || spte == sptep) {
    if (!start)
        continue;
    if (direct_pte_prefetch_many(vcpu, sp, start, spte) < 0)
        break;
    start = NULL;
}
```
Reason:
The loop only handles the case where there are non-present SPTEs preceding a present SPTE, and if the faulting GFN is a multiple of the prefetch size with all subsequent SPTEs being non-present, it fails to prefetch any trailing SPTEs, leading to increased guest page faults.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (start)
    direct_pte_prefetch_many(vcpu, sp, start, spte);
```
Reason:
This addition ensures that if there are any trailing SPTEs (i.e., SPTEs following the faulting GFN) that need to be prefetched, a final call to `direct_pte_prefetch_many()` is made, thus allowing the prefetching of these SPTEs and reducing the number of guest page faults.

